  "prefLabel": "Ph 1202.02 Central prescription processing",
  "priorExpiration": "2017-05-16",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ph 1202.02 “Central prescription processing” means “central prescription processing” as defined in RSA 318: 1, XXIII, namely, “the processing by a pharmacy of a request from another pharmacy to fill or refill a prescription drug order or to perform processing functions, such as dispensing, drug utilization review, claims adjudication, refill authorizations, and therapeutic interventions.”\n\nSource. #9469, eff 5-16-09, EXPIRED: 5-16-17\n\nNew. #12485, eff 2-24-18",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ph100-2600.html"
